\begin_layout Standard
Plugging these simulated values into Freedman's Bell parameter 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta=\vert{}R(22.5^{\circ})/R_{0}-R(67.5^{\circ})/R_{0}\vert-\frac{1}{4}$
\end_inset

 yields:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\delta\approx|{}0.3999-0.1038|-0.25=\mathbf{0.0461}>0$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This matches Freedman and Clauser's experimental measurement (
\begin_inset Formula $δ=0.050±0.008$
\end_inset

,
 or 
\begin_inset Formula $S=0.300±0.008$
\end_inset

 thereby violating the local hidden-variable bound (
\begin_inset Formula $δ≤0$
\end_inset

).
\end_layout

